(ii) Designed so that below the base flood level the structure is watertight with walls substantially impermeable to the passage of water and with structural components having the capability of resisting hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and effects of buoyancy, in accordance with the following;

(A) A registered professional engineer or architect shall develop and/or review structural design, specifications, and plans for the construction, and shall certify that the design and methods of construction are in accordance with accepted standards of practice; and

(B) A record of such certificate, which includes the specific elevation (in relation to mean sea level) to which such structures are flood proofed

