c. Every room open to the public or in which persons are employed, every public hall, and stairway in every structure shall be adequately lighted at all times that said structure is in use or open to the public. Unless otherwise provided by law, adequate lighting for the purpose of this subsection shall mean not less than five foot candles, measured at any point on the floor of a room, hall, or stairway;

